command Rose.Core.Auth : Create_Endpoint, Find_Command, Cap_Set_Service
  with Summary     => "Serve logging in and creating users.",
       Description => """
          Auth keeps the users' names and a salted hash of each password
          (#455). It returns its Auth interface, whose Login gives a
          user's User interface for the right password, and its
          Auth_Admin interface, whose New_User creates a user, with a
          home directory. It then keeps serving them. It gives each
          home directory the cap set server's Constructor, its
          Cap_Set_Service, which the directory gives each of its files
          (#867).

          A new version of the program can take over from a running one
          (ADR 0032, #831). Its state is the users: each one's name and
          password hash, and the caps it holds for each, the user's User
          interface and the Replaceable interfaces of the user's server
          and home directory, which only auth holds. Find_Command and
          Cap_Set_Service are its arguments, which the handover passes on
          (#901), so a new version is launched with Previous alone. A
          saved state has no caps, so auth with users can't be restored
          from one.
          """,
       Server      => Auth_Server.Start_Server,
       Replaceable => Auth_Server,
       Live
is
   Auth : out Auth
     with Help => "the Auth interface, for logging in";
   Admin : out Auth_Admin
     with Help => "the Auth_Admin interface, for creating users";
   Control : out Replaceable
     with Help => "its Replaceable interface";
end Rose.Core.Auth;
